    <task id="LOCAL‎-00008" summary="We updated the app.py file to support visual Track Changes for the Refine action, while preserving the existing Lantern interaction flow.&#10;&#10;Refine Button Handling (Left Panel)&#10;The Refine button now captures the response returned by handle_event.&#10;When the controller returns a refinement result (mode=&quot;refine&quot;), the returned diff_html is stored in st.session_state[&quot;last_refine_diff&quot;] instead of modifying the editor or creating a new reasoning node.&#10;&#10;Right Sidebar: Refine Diff Display&#10;A new section was added to the right sidebar that conditionally displays the stored diff_html.&#10;The changes are rendered as styled HTML (Track Changes–like visualization), clearly separated from critiques and suggested paths.&#10;&#10;User Control &amp; State Management&#10;The refinement preview is non-destructive:&#10;&#10;The editor content is not automatically modified.&#10;&#10;The reasoning tree is not altered.&#10;&#10;Users can explicitly dismiss the refinement using a dedicated button, which clears the stored diff from the session state.&#10;&#10;Preserved Interaction Semantics&#10;&#10;Expand continues to generate new reasoning paths.&#10;&#10;Critique continues to surface counter-perspectives.&#10;&#10;Refine now functions strictly as a scaffolding mechanism, providing visual suggestions without branching or overwriting content.">
